          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 09 — AI-Influenced Workflows ─────────────────────── -->
    <section class="dalx-section">
      <div class="container">

        <div class="dalx-section-head">
          <p class="dalx-section-marker">09 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Application</p>
          <h2 class="dalx-section-title">AI-Influenced Workflows</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="dalx-body dalx-body--wide">
          <p>
            The DAL-X framework applies wherever AI participates in a decision path
            that carries organizational consequence — regardless of whether the AI
            participation is agentic (the AI takes direct action) or advisory (the
            AI shapes a human decision). Consequence attaches to the decision, not
            to whether a human was formally present.
          </p>
          <p>
            The operational application of DAL-X covers both workflow types. Agentic
            AI workflows require runtime authority at the execution point — a gate
            that prevents the AI from moving forward without an active authority
            structure. Human-led AI-assisted workflows require authority mapping —
            the human reviewer must hold the authority level the AI participation
            creates at that consequence level, not merely the authority required
            for the same decision without AI involvement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="dalx-workflow-grid">

          <div class="dalx-workflow-card">
            <p class="dalx-workflow-type">Agentic AI Workflow</p>
            <p class="dalx-workflow-desc">AI takes direct action within defined scope</p>
            <div class="dalx-workflow-steps">
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">1</span>
                <span>AI agent receives task within assigned scope</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">2</span>
                <span>Trigger evaluates consequence level of proposed action</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">3</span>
                <span>Authority routing activates if threshold met</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">4</span>
                <span>Execution gate requires scope, conformance, and acknowledgment</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step dalx-wf-step--terminal">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num dalx-wf-num--orange">5</span>
                <span>Pre-execution record captured — action authorized to proceed</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="dalx-workflow-card">
            <p class="dalx-workflow-type">Human-Led AI-Assisted Workflow</p>
            <p class="dalx-workflow-desc">AI shapes the decision path; human acts on it</p>
            <div class="dalx-workflow-steps">
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">1</span>
                <span>AI produces recommendation, classification, or exception path</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">2</span>
                <span>Trigger flags AI participation and consequence level</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">3</span>
                <span>Authority routing maps to principal with matching threshold</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num">4</span>
                <span>Principal reviews with required context, evidence, and mandate</span>
              </div>
              <div class="dalx-wf-step dalx-wf-step--terminal">
                <span class="dalx-wf-num dalx-wf-num--orange">5</span>
                <span>Acknowledgment recorded — decision path authorized before action</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="dalx-statement">
          <p class="dalx-statement-text">
            "The runtime authority problem is not a technology problem. It is an
            organizational design problem — the structural void that exists when
            enterprises deploy AI systems without building the authority layer that
            governs what those systems are permitted to move toward action."
          </p>
          <p class="dalx-statement-attr">— DAL-X Framework &nbsp;·&nbsp; Jochanni Labs</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

